You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: C07
Scenario title: Evening Caregiver Handover and Next-day Preparation
Initial workflow description:
When another family member takes over in the evening, I tell them what still needs doing. We also get things ready for the next day.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "When you tell the incoming caregiver what still needs doing, is that information communicated verbally, written down, or recorded somewhere like an app or shared document?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "How do you determine which tasks still need to be done at handover time — do you work from a checklist, review a log of what was completed during the day, or rely on memory?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "Can you describe the specific steps involved in getting things ready for the next day — for example, does this include preparing medications, laying out equipment, or scheduling anything?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "Does this evening handover and preparation routine happen every day, or only on certain days, and does the content of the routine change depending on the day?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "What happens if the person taking over in the evening is unavailable or significantly delayed — is there a backup plan or does the current caregiver continue until they arrive?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "Is there any existing tool, app, or written record used during the day to track what care tasks have been completed, or is that tracking done entirely from memory?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Evening Caregiver Handover and Next-day Preparation with explicit responsibilities, decisions and recorded completion.",
  "actors": [
    "mother",
    "partner",
    "grandparent",
    "next-day caregiver"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "family handover log",
    "evening task checklist",
    "shared family calendar",
    "family messaging app"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "unfinished task list",
    "next-day schedule",
    "caregiver availability",
    "caregiver notes"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "acknowledged handover",
    "assigned remaining tasks",
    "prepared next-day items",
    "updated handover log"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "List the unfinished household care tasks",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Review the next-day schedule",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Share relevant caregiver notes with the incoming caregiver",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Confirm who accepts each remaining task",
      "actor": "grandparent"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Clarify conflicting or missing task information",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Prepare items needed for the next day",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Mark completed preparation tasks in the checklist",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Confirm unresolved tasks with the next-day caregiver",
      "actor": "mother"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Has the incoming caregiver acknowledged the remaining tasks?",
      "branches": [
        "complete the handover",
        "confirm directly before leaving tasks assigned"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Are next-day items and task owners confirmed?",
      "branches": [
        "mark preparation complete",
        "leave unresolved items open and contact the owner"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "handover note missing",
    "conflicting task information",
    "incoming caregiver unavailable",
    "next-day preparation incomplete"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A1",
      "rationale": "Draft the open-task list from checked records."
    },
    {
      "target": "A6",
      "rationale": "Generate a next-day preparation checklist."
    },
    {
      "target": "A8",
      "rationale": "Remind assigned caregivers about unresolved tasks."
    }
  ],
  "operating_context": {
    "frequency": "each evening when care responsibility changes in this fictional household",
    "manual_effort": "Updating notes and confirming tasks takes about ten minutes.",
    "data_availability": "Only participating caregivers can read the shared log; task completion is manually recorded.",
    "integration_and_approval_constraints": "A tool can summarize notes but cannot mark care performed or substitute for an acknowledged human handover."
  },
  "interpretation": "Activity dependencies describe the nominal sequence. Decision branches and exception descriptions qualify that sequence; this is not an executable BPMN model."
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
